From e784d6c915a24f1df76524bfa2c79316e1afcf1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 23:31:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 179/638] chrome: keep crash surfaces local on AROS [chromium]
 [aros]

Statement:
Chromium portable crash UI, consent, and enterprise interfaces pulled Crashpad storage and upload machinery into AROS even though the platform uses debug.resource as its baseline and OPAL for expanded context.

Decision:
Retain crash-key, chrome://crashes, consent, and enterprise API shapes. Back the upload list with the local text log, make remote enterprise forwarding inert, and exclude Crashpad-only source and dependency edges on AROS.

Evidence:
The generated Chrome project graph identified every remaining Crashpad route. The affected browser, upload-list, enterprise, and Google settings objects compile; complete crash browser/upload libraries archive successfully. A final Ninja query of chrome returns no components/crash/core/app or third_party/crashpad dependency.

Chain:

ACD-chromium-aros-native-crash-reporting
